    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0864" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg852"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.616/348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-02T19:00:00+03:00">November 2, 1941—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 3—1:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1867. For the President, the Secretary and the Under Secretary. My 1864, November
                    1, 7 p.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d800-f1"/> I called on Vyshinski today and
                    requested him to transmit to Stalin the President’s message<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d800-f2"/> which I conveyed to him orally. Vyshinski requested me to
                    leave the text with him as he said he assumed Stalin would wish to make an
                    appropriate reply. I did not feel justified in complying with his request as to
                    have done so would have compromised our Navy Department code. I have, however,
                    sent him an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> containing a carefully
                    prepared paraphrase of the message which I believe will satisfy him. If it is
                    desired that I furnish him with the text, I should appreciate instructions to
                    this effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
